<div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">How do smart irrigation controllers work in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Smart controllers use evapotranspiration sensors and local weather data to automatically adjust irrigation schedules for precise, efficient watering in Florida landscapes. As a certified Irrigreen dealer, Mr. &amp; Mrs. Outdoor Living installs systems that respond to real-time conditions — reducing overwatering and delivering measurable water savings.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bcf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">What are the benefits of drip irrigation systems?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Drip irrigation delivers water directly to plant roots, dramatically reducing evaporation, weed growth, and fungal disease in Florida landscapes. This targeted approach uses significantly less water than traditional sprinkler systems — making it ideal for South Florida homeowners navigating local water restrictions and rising utility costs.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bd7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Can smart irrigation reduce my water bill in Florida?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. Smart irrigation systems with evapotranspiration sensors prevent overwatering by adjusting schedules based on real-time weather and soil conditions. Florida homeowners who upgrade from traditional timer-based systems consistently report significant monthly water savings, with many reducing irrigation usage by 30% or more.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077bdf\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Can irrigation zones be customized for my property?</h3></div><nav class=\"dropdown-list w-dropdown-list\"><p class=\"grey\">Yes. Smart irrigation systems include individual zones designed around your property's specific plant types, soil conditions, and sun exposure. Zones can be adjusted seasonally as your landscape evolves. Our certified irrigation contractors program and test every zone before handover to ensure optimal performance across your Florida property.</p></nav></div><div data-delay=\"0\" data-hover=\"false\" data-w-id=\"9f159d33-eb67-9087-202c-bab1e4077be7\" class=\"dropdown-faq w-dropdown\"><div class=\"dropdown-toggle w-dropdown-toggle\"><div class=\"block-arrow-faq\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/close-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-close\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/images/site/open-toggle.svg\" alt=\"\" class=\"icon-dropdown-open\"></div><h3 class=\"dropdown-text\">Do you offer maintenance services after installation?</